EPIC-260715-2mqgvm_viability-and-foundation/STORY-260715-2xnj3v_apple-capability-provisioning/TASK-260715-ypo7yo_define-apple-identifier-and-entitlement-matrix/progress.md:79:2026-07-28 TASK-260728-7ii1xz AMENDMENT REQUEST (this task is the applying owner per matrix section 11). Verdict: keychain-access-groups on works.relux.tunnel.mac.tunnel KEEP PROHIBITED - promote prohibited-pending-decision to settled prohibited. The selected transport is the file-based System keychain, whose access model is per-item SecAccess ACLs, not access groups (TN3137), so the entitlement is inapplicable rather than merely unused. The provider needs no keychain entitlement: /System/Library/Sandbox/Profiles/application.sb lines 792-793 on macOS 26.5 25F71 already grant read+write on /Library/Keychains to any process holding com.apple.developer.networking.networkextension, and lines 655-656 grant the securityd Mach lookups to every sandboxed process. No new entitlement, App ID, portal capability, or C1 change. Also: M2 close OC-1 naming TASK-260728-7ii1xz; M3 downgrade OC-4 to verify-only-if-XPC-is-ever-selected since the XPC candidate was rejected; M4 no change requested on the macos.host row, recommend keep granted with purpose narrowed to iOS system of record plus macOS pre-seed staging; M5 consider a rule recording that keychain-access-groups is meaningless on the file-based path, so PureVPN shipping it cannot be used as a re-grant argument. Full rationale and evidence: TASK-260728-7ii1xz_macos-credential-transport-decision.md section 7.
EPIC-260715-2mqgvm_viability-and-foundation/STORY-260715-2xnj3v_apple-capability-provisioning/TASK-260715-ypo7yo_define-apple-identifier-and-entitlement-matrix/progress.md-80-2026-07-28 TASK-260728-7ii1xz amendment addendum M6 - com.apple.security.application-groups on both macOS targets: no value change requested, but the stated PURPOSE is wrong. The matrix section 10 traceability row host-to-provider state is an App Group snapshot plus Keychain refs, and any G2 purpose text implying a shared container on macOS, are false on macOS: the user-context host and the root provider resolve DIFFERENT containers (provider home is /private/var/root). The macOS host-to-provider channel is providerConfiguration plus the app-message seed. The entitlement is left granted because a private root-context container may still have uses this task did not survey; whether it survives least privilege is a separate review under ypo7yo ownership. See TASK-260728-7ii1xz_macos-credential-transport-decision.md sections 6 and 7.
EPIC-260715-2mqgvm_viability-and-foundation/STORY-260715-2xnj3v_apple-capability-provisioning/TASK-260715-ypo7yo_define-apple-identifier-and-entitlement-matrix/progress.md:81:2026-07-28 TASK-260728-7ii1xz r2 AMENDMENT PACKET (supersedes the r1 packet; verdict unchanged, field list now exhaustive). Target row: targets[key=macos.provider].entitlements[keychain-access-groups] on works.relux.tunnel.mac.tunnel. VERDICT: KEEP PROHIBITED. The selected transport is the file-based system-domain keychain, whose access model is per-item SecAccess ACL, not access groups (TN3137), so the entitlement is INAPPLICABLE to the mechanism used, not merely unnecessary. The provider needs no keychain entitlement at all: application.sb:792-793 on macOS 26.5 (25F71) already grants /Library/Keychains read+write to any com.apple.developer.networking.networkextension holder, and 655-656 grant the securityd Mach lookups to every sandboxed process. No value, no portal capability, no new App ID, no C1 change. FIELD-BY-FIELD (all five keys on the row): status prohibited-pending-decision -> prohibited; rationale -> the settled reason above citing TASK-260728-7ii1xz; evidence -> keep and add application.sb:792-793 plus checks E8-E10; resolutionOwner -> REMOVE (this task IS the resolution; a settled row naming a pending resolver reads as still-open); amendmentRule -> REMOVE and replace with M5. The amendmentRule removal is the critical one: its antecedent (transport gives the provider direct keychain access) is now TRUE while its consequent (amend to required with the group literal) is FALSE, so left in place it is a live instruction to re-grant the row on exactly the reasoning this decision refutes. M2: close OC-1 naming TASK-260728-7ii1xz as resolver. M3: keep OC-4 open, downgraded to verify-only-if-XPC-is-ever-selected. M4: macos.host keychain-access-groups - no change requested, recommend keep granted with the purpose narrowed to iOS system of record plus a macOS pre-seed staging item. M5: record the replacement rule - on macOS the file-based keychain is SecAccess-ACL controlled and keychain-access-groups applies only to the Data Protection Keychain, so a root-context provider never needs it and the presence of the key in a shipping third-party provider is not evidence it functions; the row reopens only if the provider is ever moved into a user context. M6: application-groups on both macOS targets - no value change, but the stated purpose and the section 10 traceability row implying a shared container on macOS are FALSE (host and provider resolve different containers). M7: bump revision, append a revisionLog entry naming TASK-260728-7ii1xz_reviewer-verdict-01.md and this decision, keep validate-matrix at exit 0, and check that deleting resolutionOwner/amendmentRule does not trip an exhaustive containment assertion - if one requires them it encoded the open state and must be updated in the same revision. Consider a negative gate: a prohibited row still carrying a resolutionOwner is a contradiction. See TASK-260728-7ii1xz_macos-credential-transport-decision.md section 7.
