EPIC-260716-3fyjn0_manual-validation-and-approvals/STORY-260716-2m2tl1_m0-viability-manual-gates/TASK-260715-3jloqy_provision-app-ids-capabilities-and-development-profiles/README.md-2-
EPIC-260716-3fyjn0_manual-validation-and-approvals/STORY-260716-2m2tl1_m0-viability-manual-gates/TASK-260715-3jloqy_provision-app-ids-capabilities-and-development-profiles/README.md-3-## Description
EPIC-260716-3fyjn0_manual-validation-and-approvals/STORY-260716-2m2tl1_m0-viability-manual-gates/TASK-260715-3jloqy_provision-app-ids-capabilities-and-development-profiles/README.md:4:Create exactly four macOS App IDs in the Relux Works Apple Developer account - works.relux.tunnel.mac, works.relux.tunnel.mac.tunnel, works.relux.tunnel.probe.mac and works.relux.tunnel.probe.mac.tunnel - enable the Network Extensions capability on all four, hosts included, and generate one Mac Development profile per App ID with this Apple-silicon Mac registered. Apple requires the packet-tunnel entitlement on the containing app as well as the embedded provider, so host App IDs are provisioned exactly like provider App IDs. No App Group record is created and the App Groups capability is enabled on nothing: rule G4 of the approved matrix (TASK-260715-ypo7yo) withholds com.apple.security.application-groups from every macOS target. There is no Keychain access-group portal mutation to perform at all, because keychain sharing has no portal record and rule K2 withholds keychain-access-groups from every macOS target. The human authorization for these mutations is granted once in Ceremony C1 (TASK-260728-q5kjta); this task is performed unattended by the agent using that granted session, and the human does not wait for it. Preserve reproducible non-secret metadata and validate each downloaded profile against the approved matrix. The four iOS identifiers stay defined in the matrix and are not provisioned on this path because iOS is deferred under ADR-024. If the portal forces a fresh two-factor challenge mid-run, record it as a named short re-authentication interaction rather than silently retrying.
